 "notes": "Observed 95% CL upper limits on |d_e| from Fig. 4 (vector paths in e-print file PlotdeLimTotal.pdf). Paper's Eq. (1) uses L = (d_e kappa phi/4e^2) F^2 with kappa=sqrt(4 pi G_N), identical to the canonical Damour-Donoghue d_e; no conversion needed. Fig. 4 shows two observed curves: LT data 2010-2012 (red, m ~ 6.6e-25 to 6.5e-21 eV) and ST data 19 Oct 2012 (blue, m ~ 2.6e-21 to 8.3e-16 eV). Reported curve is the lower envelope: LT below 6.5e-21 eV, ST above (a step up occurs at the junction near 6e-21 eV). Wiggly observed curves were bin-medianed (~0.1 dex bins). Axis calibration cross-checked against the figure's top omega axis (agrees to 0.02 dex). Assumes phi is all of the DM with rho_DM = 0.3 GeV/cm^3; expected-limit bands not used.",
